@startuml wiring-overview
top to bottom direction
title LocalAiRobot — Power & Signal Wiring (one 3S LiPo: ESC drive + buck 7.4V/UPS to the Pi)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 17
skinparam TitleFontSize 21
skinparam ArrowFontSize 14
skinparam rectangle {
  FontSize 17
  BorderColor #333333
}

package "POWER  (single 3S LiPo)" #ffe6e6 {
  rectangle "3S LiPo\n11.1V" as LIPO
  rectangle "Kill switch\n(inline loop)" as KILL
  rectangle "ESC\n(brushed crawler)" as ESC
  rectangle "540 35T\nbrushed motor" as MOTOR
  rectangle "Adjustable buck\n(SZBK07 / XL4016)\n3S -> 7.4V, >=8A" as UBEC
}

package "BRAIN RAIL  (5V / 3.3V, via buck -> UPS)" #e6f0ff {
  rectangle "Raspberry Pi 5\n(buck 7.4V -> UPS HAT / 27W PSU bench)" as PI
  rectangle "PCA9685\nPWM @ 0x40" as PCA
  rectangle "Steering servo\n(FRONT only, ch1)" as SERVO
}

LIPO  --> KILL  : red (+) / black (-)
KILL  --> ESC   : battery in
KILL  --> UBEC  : 11.1V tap
UBEC  --> PI    : 7.4V -> UPS input (UPS -> clean 5.1V)
ESC   --> MOTOR : blue + yellow\n(2-wire brushed)
ESC   --> PCA   : 3-wire lead\nsignal -> ch0 PWM\nred -> V+ rail (ESC BEC)\nblack -> ch0 GND
PCA   --> SERVO : ch1\nPWM / V+ / GND
PI    --> PCA   : 3.3V VCC\nSDA=GPIO2 / SCL=GPIO3\nGND  (I2C)

note bottom
  ONE 3S LiPo feeds both the ESC (drive + servo BEC) AND an adjustable buck @ 7.4V -> the Pi's UPS input (18650 backup).
  COMMON GROUND BUS:  Pi GND  <->  PCA9685 GND  <->  ESC GND  <->  buck GND.
  The ESC BEC (on ch0 V+) powers the whole V+ rail -> the ch1 servo (use an HV servo).
  Use an ADJUSTABLE switching buck (SZBK07 / XL4016, >=8A) set to 7.4V; a fixed 5-6V UBEC sags ~0.5V under load and
  browns the Pi 5 out. The UPS re-regulates a clean 5.1V; the kill switch cuts drive but the UPS keeps the Pi up. Never feed the UPS above 8.4V.
end note
@enduml
